BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/snakes-of-the-blue-ridge/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260508T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260508T143000
DTSTAMP:20260508T122422
CREATED:20260323T173833Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260323T173953Z
UID:10017005-1778245200-1778250600@www.ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Snakes of the Blue Ridge
DESCRIPTION:Snakes of the Blue Ridge\nwith Patrick Brannon \nFriday\, May 8  |  1 – 2:30pm \nBRN – Elective \nREGISTER HERE \nParticipants in this workshop will learn about the general biology of snakes\, including the natural history and identification of many Southern Appalachian snake species. We will discuss the differences between venomous and non-venomous species\, as well as dispelling many common misconceptions about snakes. \nPatrick Brannon is an independent naturalist and educator. He holds a M.S. in Biology from Appalachian State University\, and has performed research on the ecology of salamanders and small mammals. For the past 22 years he was Outreach Coordinator at the WCU Highlands Biological Station\, where he taught courses on amphibians and mammals as part of the UNC Institute for the Environment Program at HBS\, in addition to many K-12 school programs and educator workshops. \n\nMembers: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions.\nSee a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs.\nWe are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide.\nFollow us on Facebook & Instagram!\nJoin our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord!\nInterested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here.\n\nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/snakes-of-the-blue-ridge/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Adult-Ed-Course-Jpgs-18.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/naturalist-walk-and-talk-native-orchids/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260508T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260508T150000
DTSTAMP:20260508T122422
CREATED:20260323T160436Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260323T160455Z
UID:10017003-1778245200-1778252400@www.ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Naturalist Walk and Talk – Native Orchids
DESCRIPTION:Naturalist Walk and Talk – Native Orchids\nwith Shane Myers \nFriday\, May 8  |  1 – 3pm \nBRN –  Elective \nREGISTER HERE \nWalk around the Arboretum with our staff naturalists and talk about what we see around us. We might see plants and animals\, and evidence of them going about their lives in our backyard. Topics will be based on what we see and experience and whatever questions that come up\, so every class has the potential to be quite different. \nThis program will take place outside and will follow easy trails and paved walkways. Dress for the weather and prepare to be outside for the entire program time. \nShane Myers’ interest in nature began as a child with a love of dinosaurs. This quickly grew to include fossils\, insects\, and reptiles\, and learning from the notes his grandparents kept of the birds that came to their feeders in Toledo\, Ohio.  He has a Bachelors of Science in Wildlife Biology and did most of his undergraduate work on dragonflies and damselflies. This work included coordinating an Ohio- wide survey of dragonflies that culminated in a publication in 2024. He’s assisted in outreach and education for plant conservation groups\, Odonata Groups\, and various bird groups. Shane currently works for the Adult Education department at the NC Arboretum. \n\nMembers: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions.\nSee a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs.\nWe are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide.\nFollow us on Facebook & Instagram!\nJoin our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord!\nInterested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here.\n\nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/naturalist-walk-and-talk-native-orchids/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/InterpretiveWalk.jpg
END:VEVENT
