X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Haywood County Walking Meetup Group": "https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/events/314607905/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_haywood_county_walking_meetup_group
X-SOURCE:Haywood County Walking Group
UID:event_314607905@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260509T034757Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260509T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260509T160000
SUMMARY:Choose a 5 KM or 10 KM City Walk in Greenville SC
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nThere is a large parking 
 garage just behind the Westin Hotel\, 120 South Main St.\, Greenville.\n\n
 There is also a free parking lot on the roof of the building at the corner
  of W North St. and Richardson St. Walk from the south side of the parking
  lot to Main St. Turn right on Main and go 3 blocks to Joel's Java Coffee 
 Shop (next to the Westin Hotel).\n\nWe'll gather and register at Joel's Ja
 va Coffee Shop at 12:30 p.m. It is National Butterscotch Brownie Day. Perh
 aps Joel's will have some for purchase. You'll surely want to try one of t
 heir treats at any rate.\n\nWe are doing this walk with the Asheville Ambl
 ers\, AARP\, Stryder\, and perhaps others. The walk is free\, although the
  Amblers do accept donations ($4 suggested donation). Step-off is at 1:00.
 \n\nChoose between a 5 KM guided walk and a 10 KM guided walk. Both walks 
 have some moderate hills and stair climbing and are mostly on pavement.\n\
 nBoth walks include a beautiful stroll through Falls Park with spectacular
  falls and along the Reedy River. You will take in part of the Swamp Rabbi
 t Trail. The walk also takes you down both sides of Main Street\, where yo
 u'll try to find the little brass mice hidden there. The 10 KM walk also i
 ncludes a fine neighborhood\, a large park with shaded and open trails\, t
 he zoo\, and more of the Swamp Rabbit Trail.\n\nDress for the weather\; co
 nsider a hat and sunscreen. Tennis shoes will be fine. Walking sticks are 
 not needed by most. Bring a protein snack and plenty of water. Take care o
 f restroom needs before the walk\; the 10 KM walk passes restrooms at the 
 zoo. Strollers and wheelchairs are not recommended.\n\nGreenville is a won
 derful\, family-friendly city. Many will want to come early for lunch at o
 ne of the many wonderful restaurants along Main Street. Some may want to e
 xplore more after the walk and perhaps stay for supper. Plan to enjoy your
  visit.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/314607905/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260503T115916Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260503T115916Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
