UID:10017220-1778338800-1778346000@www.ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:New Growth: Artists Respond to the Forest Closing Reception
DESCRIPTION:New Growth: Artists Respond to the Forest Closing Reception\nMay 9\, 2026\n3:00 – 5:00 p.m.\nJoin us as we celebrate our inaugural season of Resident Artists and bid farewell to this spectacular exhibit. This event is open to the public. \nSpring Resident Artists \nLynn Fister is an installation artist\, musician and writer. Her work draws inspiration from fairy tales and surrealism. Lynn is creating an installation called ‘Pink Liminal Forest’ that incorporates dried plant material and textiles that she has hand dyed with custom botanical dyes. Lynn creates installations with her Drones In The Garden art collective\, and performs music as Farewell Phoenix.  \nLiz Williams is a photographer and digital media artist. Liz is creating an installation that will include video projection of photographs of the site and microscope slide images of plants that are currently blooming. You can find more of Liz’s work at the Asheville Art Museum and the Atlanta Contemporary Museum of Art.
URL:https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/new-growth-artists-respond-to-the-forest-closing-reception/
LOCATION:Baker Exhibit Center
CATEGORIES:Events
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/20260404_lewis_exhibits__064.jpg
END:VEVENT
